From: Denys Vitali <denys@denv.it>
Subject: [PATCH] egl/dri2: pvr: do not advertise EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import_modifiers

mutter creates its zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 global only when this extension is
present. With it, EGL Wayland clients on the SGX540 either get killed
(explicit DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID import fails) or, with that worked around, crash
gnome-shell inside libGLESv2_PVR_MESA.so. Without it, clients use wl_drm.
EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import itself is kept.
---
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c	2026-11-19 22:34:03.730668156 +0000
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c	2026-11-19 23:27:04.736566299 +0000
@@ -1003,7 +1003,11 @@
       if (dri2_dpy->image->base.version >= 8 &&
           dri2_dpy->image->createImageFromDmaBufs) {
          disp->Extensions.EXT_image_dma_buf_import = EGL_TRUE;
-         disp->Extensions.EXT_image_dma_buf_import_modifiers = EGL_TRUE;
+         /* pvr: not advertised. mutter only exposes zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 when
+          * it is present. Client dmabufs imported through that path crash the
+          * SGX blob in the compositor (libGLESv2_PVR_MESA, NULL deref), while
+          * the wl_drm (EGL_WL_bind_wayland_display) path is what the PVR stack
+          * was built around. */
       }
 #endif
    }
